  "headline": "The chemically load-bearing quantity for a two-part epoxy-amine coating is the amine-H:epoxide equivalents index r=(m_B*EEW)/(m_A*AHEW), not the raw mass ratio. First-principles AHEW is derived for 7/7 pure-amine hardeners (all in published band). The mass-envelope-induced index excursion is EEW/AHEW-invariant at +10.5263%/-9.5238% (10/10 envelopes), its GUM tolerance STRICTLY exceeds the mass-only 7.0711% once equivalent-weight uncertainty is admitted, and BOTH amine-rich and amine-lean corners pass all three shipped hard gates (10/10). The shipped 3-constraint envelope bounds neither extreme of the index.",
