  "purpose": "Extend the envelope->ratio gap from the raw mass ratio to the chemically correct amine-hydrogen:epoxide equivalents stoichiometric index r=(m_B*EEW)/(m_A*AHEW); derive first-principles AHEW for the 7 pure-amine hardeners, prove the index excursion is EEW/AHEW-invariant, extend the GUM budget with equivalent-weight uncertainty, and confirm the shipped envelope bounds neither the amine-rich nor amine-lean corner of the stoichiometric index.",
  "run_type": "independent_non_runtime_theory_axis",
  "schema": "amphora.envelope-gates.stoichiometric-index-equivalents-diagnostic.v1",
  "study_id": "stoichiometric-index-equivalents-v1",
  "theory_reference": [
    "Lee, H. & Neville, K., 'Handbook of Epoxy Resins', McGraw-Hill 1967, Ch.5-6 (epoxide equivalent weight EEW, amine-hydrogen equivalent weight AHEW, stoichiometric mix calculation).",
    "Ellis, B. (ed.), 'Chemistry and Technology of Epoxy Resins', Blackie 1993, Ch.6 (stoichiometric amine:epoxide balance, off-stoichiometry).",
    "May, C.A. (ed.), 'Epoxy Resins: Chemistry and Technology', 2nd ed., Marcel Dekker 1988, Ch.4 (off-stoichiometry effect on network Tg).",
